Subject: [PATCH 08535/11362] fix(arc): re-measure the worst-case induce-prompt
 token count under current defaults

Continues the 2026-08-08 adversarial live-agent review fix pass.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6227 (Correctness finding 5): _INDUCE_WORST_CASE_PROMPT_TOKENS
was measured 2026-07-28 at k=8 transitions with no object table. Neither is
the shipped default any more: k defaults to ALL transitions (2026-08-01),
and the object-perception table is default ON (2026-08-07). Re-measured
through the real gemma-4-31B-it Q4_K_M GGUF tokenizer, same methodology as
the predecessor measurement: 22352 tokens under current defaults, +41.8%
over the stale 15767, and it EXCEEDS the old per-slot budget (81920/4-4096
= 16384 tokens) by 5968 tokens -- a real overflow risk at K=4 concurrency.
_default_induce_n_ctx() derives the new pool size automatically: 106496.
The Kaggle kernel's own concurrency preflight probe imports the constant
directly, so it inherits the fix with no separate kernel-side edit.

Consequence discovered and honestly resolved: local 24GB-3090 dev no
longer auto-fits the worst-case prompt at all, even at max FFN offload --
confirmed by a real launch attempt (cudaMalloc OOM) and a real per-PID
VRAM measurement via offload-and-reconstruct (25123.6 MiB, within 0.4 MiB
of the linear model's own prediction). This is a genuine physical
constraint, not a regression to paper over; the documented
CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_N_CTX override remains the local-dev remedy. The Kaggle
SCORED path (96GB) is unaffected, confirmed by its own pre-existing test
passing unchanged. Three tests retargeted accordingly, with dated
correction docstrings preserving the original reasoning.

Tests: test_arc_induce_worst_case_prompt_tokens_20260808.py (3 new tests,
pinning the constant, the derived n_ctx, and that the new worst case
genuinely exceeds the old budget). Updated: test_arc_generator_vram_guard.py,
test_arc_ffn_cpu_offload.py, test_arc_generator_migration_defects.py.
Broader sweep: 131 passed across the generator/VRAM-guard/FFN-offload/
migration-defects/kaggle-machine-shape/liveness-witness test areas.

Also files ops/known-issues.md with 19 test failures found during this
sweep, confirmed (via a clean detached-HEAD worktree) to be pre-existing
and unrelated to this fix pass -- not touched here, flagged for separate
investigation.

